00:19:17.356 --> 00:19:21.140
So at the beginning,
bringing him back to the story and

00:19:21.140 --> 00:19:24.610
why it's part of this
sharing your story series.

00:19:24.610 --> 00:19:27.197
You've had an opportunity to think big.

00:19:27.197 --> 00:19:29.581
What are the things that
you're looking towards?

00:19:29.581 --> 00:19:31.555
What is on your horizon?

00:19:31.555 --> 00:19:33.115
For traditional interviews,

00:19:33.115 --> 00:19:36.295
you are going to be asked about
your opinions, your thoughts,

00:19:36.295 --> 00:19:40.323
maybe there might be a hypothetical
situation or something along those lines.

00:19:40.323 --> 00:19:43.948
At Stanford we're going to be focusing
on behavioral basic questions.

00:19:43.948 --> 00:19:46.617
We're really going to be
asking you about your past.

00:19:46.617 --> 00:19:48.921
The footsteps that you've
gotten to get here.

00:19:48.921 --> 00:19:50.884
What did that path look like?

00:19:50.884 --> 00:19:52.574
What was the environment and

00:19:52.574 --> 00:19:56.952
the circumstances that shaped the way
that you got to where you are today?

00:19:56.952 --> 00:20:02.737
So really specific anecdotes,
examples and experiences.

00:20:02.737 --> 00:20:07.970
The great thing about this is that
you are already the expert in you.

00:20:07.970 --> 00:20:11.912
And so from here it's not about
having to think forward and hey,

00:20:11.912 --> 00:20:13.591
does this plan make sense?

00:20:13.591 --> 00:20:18.734
But really think backwards,
reflect and remember.

00:20:18.734 --> 00:20:24.240
So, here are a few tips and
best practices as we enter the process.

00:20:24.240 --> 00:20:27.252
So, remember, reflect, process, connect,

00:20:27.252 --> 00:20:30.855
uses this phrase at least once
in each one of the sessions.

00:20:30.855 --> 00:20:37.213
Remember instances from your past,
reflect on the circumstances around it.

00:20:37.213 --> 00:20:38.249
What led to it?

00:20:38.249 --> 00:20:39.567
What happened?

00:20:39.567 --> 00:20:41.484
Who was involved?

00:20:41.484 --> 00:20:45.700
Process, how did that
connect to the greater whole?

00:20:45.700 --> 00:20:47.854
What were the things that you did?

00:20:47.854 --> 00:20:49.435
The how's and the whys.

00:20:49.435 --> 00:20:51.552
Now that hindsight is 2020.

00:20:51.552 --> 00:20:54.483
Let's process the way those
things work together.

00:20:54.483 --> 00:20:59.387
So you actually got from point A to point
B, or maybe you got from point A to

00:20:59.387 --> 00:21:03.972
lowercase a stalled a little bit,
went back to the drawing board and

00:21:03.972 --> 00:21:07.614
then got to a different version of B and
then connect.

00:21:07.614 --> 00:21:09.673
Connect the dots between
the different things.

00:21:09.673 --> 00:21:15.132
If there was learning that happened where
else might you have applied that learning?

00:21:15.132 --> 00:21:17.315
Have there been themes?

00:21:17.315 --> 00:21:18.722
How did that theme emerge?

00:21:18.722 --> 00:21:22.748
Or if there was a really important
strategic insight you had,

00:21:22.748 --> 00:21:24.457
did you have another one?

00:21:24.457 --> 00:21:25.263
Where was it?

00:21:25.263 --> 00:21:29.083
What were the things that kind of
sparked that experience for you?

00:21:29.083 --> 00:21:33.434
So, remember, reflect, process, connect.

00:21:33.434 --> 00:21:38.402
So a non exhaustive list of things
that you might want to think about,

00:21:38.402 --> 00:21:43.197
how do you narrow down that list
of possible life experiences that

00:21:43.197 --> 00:21:45.217
you want to like brush up on?

00:21:45.217 --> 00:21:47.338
So a few things to think about.

00:21:47.338 --> 00:21:49.638
What are things that you're proud of?

00:21:49.638 --> 00:21:54.096
This can be both in your professional
life, your personal life,

00:21:54.096 --> 00:21:57.107
